; Stage 15 W9 item 13's everyday manifestation, and the reason the fix routes
; through `unknown-type-message` instead of inventing a message here: a
; parametric type whose template is real but whose file was never imported.
; `(Vector i32)` without `(import-use vector)` reported "missing :type on param
; 'x'" — blaming the one thing that is unambiguously present in the source.
;
; Reusing the tiered message means this spelling gets the reachability note for
; free, the same note a bare unknown type has had since W1c.
;
; Compiling this must FAIL naming the file that does define it:
;   "'Vector' is defined in lib/vector.nuch, which no import in this unit reaches"
(defn f (x:(Vector i32)):i32
  (return 0))

(defn main ():i32
  (return 0))
